        "postDate": "2026-10-31T07:14:04.390Z",
        "rawMarkdown": "I’m a student in my second competition. I’ve reproduced the public 0.66 recipe and tested a few changes (hard punctuation rules, softer balancing, pseudo-labelling the n-gram SVM, wider ATLAS coverage); all came out within the rerun noise. For those above 0.70, without revealing your solution: is the gap mainly data (more in-style passages per model) or modelling? Any general direction would really help someone learning. Thanks!",
